Lattice tests of S's per-loop coefficients (model_s_results 36); 512 loop rows, shelf pole a = 0.916883
Z: precision-weighted Rayleigh (any offset), weights from take noise + read bias; p_an = exp(-Z); p_rand: random spacings within x1.6
(powers of two excluded), the look-elsewhere-safe p; Z_on: the Z a true grid would give with take noise only / with the read bias too
(bias: the sd of this read minus the _lowrt baseline's read of the same takes, per RT step; a lower bound); b/q: that bias over the step.
phi: the phase (0 = grid points at k 2^-n). Held out by setting: the phase found on LF 0.1 / 1.0 tested on LF 0.4 / 2.0 and vice versa, z.
A / B phase z (take A's phase on take B): ~ sqrt(2 Z) whenever q >> take noise, so it shows only that the values are reproducible, not a lattice.

